WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.933
A closing diphthong moves the tongue toward a second vowel position, as in the /aʊ/

00:00:06.933 --> 00:00:10.973
of now and /əʊ/ of go (in many accents).

00:00:11.783 --> 00:00:16.967
Which word has the closing diphthong /aʊ/ (as in now)? Answer: cow

00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:23.000
Read several examples of the closing diphthongs in now and go, paying attention to

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:23.373
pronunciation.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.461
Cow shares the gliding vowel in now.
